  "disposition": [
    "Core owns the exhaustive live/inert fiber suspension and original Source admissions. Program fanout state and scheduler are cohesive child modules of those owners; no I/O or higher-layer dependency is added. The shared AwaitMany site proof remains on FrameValueContext, avoiding duplicated admission logic.",
    "ProductStep owns real worker lifetime, registry receipts and Ready transfers. The new module does not introduce a Host base or duplicate capture authority; free captures remain in the original frame. Existing large fiber/line/product owners remain cohesive state-machine/schema visitors and consumers of the same exhaustive suspension grammar.",
    "Codegen owns compiled transition validation; the metadata-only notice migrates its actual VM mapping and dispatcher together. Compiler and runtime-plan fixtures follow the real consumer/lowering boundaries. Splitting these consumers only for numeric LOC would widen internal APIs without a new owner."
